1. modify the HOME macro in make.inc to point to where crd-fasteig is installed

2. Define the locations of 
   MKL
   eigen

3. Set compiler and compiler flags


Then do

make lib 

to generate a libfasteig_$(PLAT).a where PLAT is a user defined Platform name, e.g., Perlmutter


To run some examples


cd examples

make 

generates an executable called 'runfasteig'

Run the executable by the following command


./runfasteig  SiO.input

where SiO.input is an input file that contains a list of problem descriptions


amatrix ./Sparse_Matrices/SiO.mtx
logfile SiO
nev     5
which   SR
solver  Chebyshev
maxiter 10
maxdim  20
degree  8
tol     1e-6
